ces in the Football League, scoring 61 times.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d00\", \"start\": 588, \"end\": 606, \"text\": \"In August 2000, he\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 436, \"text\": \"[ 1 ] Date of birth ( 1961-12-04 ) 4 December 1961 ( age 63 ) [ 1 ] Place of birth Manchester , [ 1 ] England Height 6 ft 2 in ( 1.88 m ) [ 2 ] Position ( s ) Defender Youth career Ashton United [ 3 ] Senior career * Years Team Apps ( Gls ) 1979–1981 Manchester City 0 ( 0 ) 1981–1984 Cardiff City 87 ( 11 ) 1984–1995 Sunderland 369 ( 23 ) 1995–1996 Carlisle United 26 ( 5 ) 1996–1998 Scarborough 87 ( 18 ) 1998–2000 Darlington 34 ( 4 )\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 125, \"text\": \"Gary Bennett (footballer, born 1961) Gary Ernest Bennett (born 4 December 1961) is an English former professional footballer.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d02\", \"start\": 126, \"end\": 219, \"text\": \"A forward, he began his career with Manchester City before moving on to Cardiff City in 1981.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d02\", \"start\": 220, \"end\": 370, \"text\": \"In 1984, Bennett joined Sunderland and he went on to make over 350 appearances for the club, placing him fifth on the club's all-time appearance list.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d02\", \"start\": 371, \"end\": 497, \"text\": \"He left Sunderland in 1995, after eleven years at the club, and later played for Carlisle United, Scarborough, and Darlington.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0064-eeaaacf08fc8:d02\", \"start\": 498, \"end\": 587, \"text\": \"During his career, he made over 600 appearances in the Football League, scoring 61 times.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"d